    "summary": "Hardwood club (used for fish ?), more fully three dimensional than nos.23 and 24 in collection, carved with the form of a sea monster, such as a sea wolf, the head well executed with open mouth, teeth including large canines, eyes ears and nostrils in accomplished formline design, the paws/flippers also in formline design, with a raised curved wolf-like tail. The handle is straight, circular cross section ending in a raised flatt butt, this finial with one deeply incised line around the circumference.",
